 "honest": [
  "both books equal-weight the entire live universe (pick_n=9999), so this census measures the eligibility flow and not a top-N selection rule",
  "the overlap rows compare each month-end decision with the nearest weekly session; where those coincide the overlap is exact by construction and the coincident pairs are counted separately, not averaged away",
  "stale_hold is truncated at the window ends -- the last exit of the series has no following decision and is never counted",
  "`week_near_me` reuses the same pairing as the nearest-weekly read, deduped on the weekly session, because that is exactly how its calendar is built",
  "membership_reading is a 0.95 flat threshold on the mean overlap: a label, not a test, and no prereg covers it",
  "decisions priced on a mid-arrival bar or on an empty cash book (live count collapsing against its neighbours) are dropped and counted in spec.dropped_decisions -- without that guard one unfinished session reads as a +1200-name entrant wave",
  "an era missing from the pair table was dropped as a cash/stub block, not censused as perfect agreement: the eligibility burn-in leaves the early window in cash, the same cash-slice signature E59/E64 print as an exact 0.0bp gap",
  "descriptive census only: no gate, no verdict, no ledger booking, trial 0"
 ]
